cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Probity: a low-cost vision model reads the document, a state machine with rules decides"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mancilla Montero"
    given-names: "Javier"
    affiliation: "SquareOne Labs"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/maximer-v/probity
abstract: >-
  A framework for extracting structured data from scanned and photographed financial
  documents. An inexpensive vision model transcribes each page; rules implemented as code
  check the transcription with exact arithmetic; where a rule fails, a different model
  re-reads that page blind and code decides between the two readings. Each document is
  reported as confirmed, inconsistent at a named row, or unresolved, with every corrected
  value recorded.
keywords:
  - bank statements
  - document extraction
  - reconciliation
  - verification
  - provenance
